---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Placeholder from '../components/Placeholder.astro';
import { url } from '../config';
---

<Base
  title="Services"
  description="Preventive maintenance management, vendor coordination, compliance and documentation, and transparent owner reporting for yachts in Newport Harbor."
  path="/services"
  heading="Services"
  kind="hub"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Services</p>
      <h1>What management actually covers.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Four services that work as one system. The maintenance schedule drives
        the vendor work, the vendor work produces the record, and the record
        becomes your monthly report.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">01 — Preventive maintenance management</p>
      <h2>A schedule built from your vessel, not a generic checklist.</h2>
      <p>
        We start from what is actually installed on your boat — engines,
        generator, watermaker, HVAC, electronics, hull and running gear — and
        build the service schedule from those specific systems.
      </p>
      <p>
        Intervals are tracked two ways at once: by calendar date and by engine
        hours, because a boat that ran 300 hours this season needs a different
        schedule from one that ran 40. Each upcoming item carries lead time, so
        haul-outs, bottom work, and running-gear service get scheduled before
        they are due rather than after.
      </p>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>Full systems inventory with make, model, serial, and hour readings</li>
        <li>Service intervals tracked by both calendar time and engine hours</li>
        <li>Lead-time alerting so scheduled work is booked in advance</li>
        <li>Condition noted and photographed at each visit</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="notice">
        <p>
          <strong>Service intervals:</strong>
          <Placeholder key="intervals" label="the specific intervals Anchor Point commits to per system — to be set by the CEO / Head of Marine Operations, not published until confirmed" />
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">02 — Vendor coordination</p>
      <h2>Someone meets the trade at the boat.</h2>
      <p>
        Most of the friction in yacht ownership is not the repair — it is
        arranging the repair. Getting a quote, matching a schedule, being at the
        slip when the technician arrives, and confirming afterwards that the
        work was actually done to standard.
      </p>
      <p>
        We take that end to end. We scope the job, arrange the contractor,
        attend the work where attendance matters, and check the result before
        the invoice is approved.
      </p>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>Job scoped and quoted before work is authorised</li>
        <li>Scheduling handled directly with the trade</li>
        <li>Attendance at the vessel for work that warrants it</li>
        <li>Completion checked and photographed before invoice approval</li>
        <li>Costs captured against the vessel record as the work closes</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="notice">
        <p>
          <strong>Spend authority:</strong>
          <Placeholder key="spendThreshold" label="the dollar threshold below which Anchor Point may authorise work without owner approval" />
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">03 — Compliance &amp; documentation</p>
      <h2>Renewal dates tracked ahead of the deadline.</h2>
      <p>
        Vessel documentation, registration, and insurance all run on renewal
        cycles that are easy to lose track of and unpleasant to discover late.
        We hold those dates alongside the maintenance schedule and raise them
        before they expire.
      </p>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>Registration and vessel documentation renewal dates tracked</li>
        <li>Insurance renewal and survey deadlines calendared with lead time</li>
        <li>Service records retained and organised per vessel</li>
        <li>Documentation assembled for survey, sale, or insurance review</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="notice">
        <p>
          We track deadlines and assemble records. We do not provide legal,
          insurance, or regulatory advice.
          <Placeholder key="complianceScope" label="confirm exact compliance scope and any disclaimer wording required by counsel or insurer" />
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">04 — Transparent owner reporting</p>
      <h2>A written record, every month.</h2>
      <p>
        This is the part we care most about. An owner should never have to send
        a text asking what happened with their boat.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every month you receive a report covering the work completed that
        period, the work scheduled next, the current state of your vessel's
        systems, and the costs incurred — with photographs of the work as
        evidence, not just line items.
      </p>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>Monthly vessel report covering work done, work upcoming, and spend</li>
        <li>Photo documentation attached to completed work</li>
        <li>Running service history retained for the life of the engagement</li>
        <li>Costs itemised per job rather than bundled into a single figure</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="notice">
        <p>
          <strong>Online owner portal:</strong> a real-time portal is in
          development. Reporting is delivered as a written monthly report until
          it ships.
          <Placeholder key="portalTiming" label="confirm whether to mention the portal publicly, and any timing you want stated" />
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="eyebrow">Engagement &amp; fees</p>
        <h2>How management is priced.</h2>
        <p>
          Fee structure:
          <Placeholder key="pricing" label="management fee structure — monthly retainer, per-foot rate, or tiers" />
        </p>
        <p>
          Agreement terms:
          <Placeholder key="terms" label="contract length, notice period, and what is included vs. billed separately" />
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href={url('/contact')}>Request a Consultation</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href={url('/how-it-works')}>See the onboarding process</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
